# Assigned cell: mode=menus, view=1280x800, save=carried (menus has no
# boss/spec/style axis). #273 means carried behaves as fresh here (own port,
# own localStorage), so this is really a fresh save on desktop/mouse.
#
# This exact view/save pairing has been hit twice before (2026-09-26T05:00,
# 2026-09-26T18:45), both chasing the Escape/p key bug. Trying new ground
# instead: README's "Getting in" section claims the party (composition)
# screen draws a locked entry for anything past the tank/healer caps ("a
# third tank or a fourth healer cannot be selected on the party screen at
# all -- the entry is drawn locked"). No prior menus session has actually
# pressed a spec tile on this screen to test that claim; only slot:1 was
# ever tapped once (2026-09-25-9), to open a picker and look, never to
# change anything. Reading src/render/composition.ts first: drawComposition
# draws every spec tile identically (only `chosen` gets a highlight) --
# there is no per-tile disabled/locked visual state in the draw code at all,
# and `hitComposition` answers every tile the same way regardless of
# legality. The actual gate is downstream, in `compose.ts`'s `pressSpec` ->
# `selectInto`: an illegal pick sets `c.refused` to a sentence drawn on the
# note line *after* the tap, not before it. So the claim to test is not
# "does a bad pick get refused" (it should) but "is the entry drawn locked
# beforehand", which this screen's own source says it is not.
#
# Start short and look before committing to which slot to press.
open
tap raid
targets
shot raidsetup
tap next
targets
shot classpick
tap compose
targets
ui
shot compose-initial

# Default roster already sits at the tank cap: Nara (slot:6, warrior tank)
# and Pike (slot:8, druid tank) are two tanks, matching "2 tanks" in the
# summary line. Open the player's own dps slot and look at the spec list
# before pressing anything -- if README's "drawn locked" claim holds, a
# tank spec tile should look different (dimmed/disabled) from here.
tap slot:0
targets
shot compose-slot0-open

# Press a tank spec anyway. If the game truly draws locked entries, this
# tap should not even register as that tile (or should be a no-op with no
# visible change). If instead it registers, refuses, and only *then* prints
# a sentence, that is the opposite of "cannot be selected... drawn locked".
tap spec:warrior:protection
targets
shot compose-after-3rd-tank

# Confirm the slot itself did not change (still Mage), then try the same
# thing on a second dps slot with the other tank-capable pick to see if the
# refusal is a one-off or the same every time.
tap slot:2
targets
shot compose-slot2-open
tap spec:paladin:protection
targets
shot compose-after-3rd-tank-again

# Close the picker and confirm the refused pick never touched the slot.
tap dismiss
targets
shot compose-dismissed
